**Done** — Created all 8 components in `src/components/content/`, each with a house-style header doc-comment, CSS-var scoped styles, and the `.figure-plate`/`thread-beat` corner-tick / `lift-hover` vocabulary where the spec called for a boxed treatment:
- `ExecutiveSignal.astro`, `RevisionNote.astro`, `BoundaryGrid.astro`, `ImplementationStatus.astro`, `ReceiptDisclosure.astro`, `ClaimBadge.astro`, `RelatedWork.astro`, `PullQuote.astro`

**Prop interfaces** match COMPONENT-API.md §5-12 exactly — no deviations.

**Design calls not fully pinned by the API doc** (documented in each file's header):
- `ClaimBadge` wraps `<Evidence kind={kind} />` internally (per the doc's explicit option) rather than re-exporting the map — zero duplication.
- `RevisionNote`'s "thin single line" is achieved by collapsing the note text itself behind the `<details>` trigger (only "Revised {date} · What's changed?" shows at rest) — the doc didn't specify exactly what stays visible vs. collapsed, and a always-visible full note would risk wrapping past one line.
- `ImplementationStatus` chips reuse `Callout.astro`'s existing 4-color Tailwind semantic palette (emerald/amber/violet/sky) rather than CSS vars, since that's the established precedent for multi-state semantic chips in this codebase; status text is always rendered so color is never the sole cue.
- `PullQuote` deliberately has no `lift-hover` (noted inline) since it's typographic, not a card; `thesis-marker` renders a `<p>`, not a `<blockquote>`, since it's a stated claim.
- `BoundaryGrid` reused the corner-tick language per the doc's explicit "leg's call" option.

**Verified:** `nvm use 22 && npm run check` — 2637 pre-existing baseline errors, zero in any of the 8 new files (grepped by filename).

**Left for other legs:** wiring these into `PostLayout.astro`/`PostSidebar.astro`/the MDX manuscript — out of my scope by design.
